# Suppressions for the trivy image scan. The CI gate runs with
# --ignore-unfixed, so it already fails only on vulnerabilities that HAVE a
# fix; this file removes two remaining classes of unactionable noise.
#
# Reviewed: 2026-09-11

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Unfixed base-image CVEs — Debian trixie (python:3.12-slim).
#    Every entry is `fixed: none` upstream. They live in packages the
#    workloads never invoke: perl is never executed, no setuid binary is
#    used, no interactive login exists. Re-review when the base is bumped.

# perl-base — no perl in any code path
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-8376

# util-linux / mount / login / bsdutils — setuid mount/login CVEs; containers
# run as non-root with no setuid use.
CVE-2024-28085
CVE-2025-5222

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. pip's vendored copies (pip/_vendor/): pip bundles its own msgpack and
#    setuptools, pinned old in pip/_vendor/vendor.txt. The *runtime* packages
#    the app imports are patched (msgpack 1.2.2, setuptools 84.0.0 — verified
#    in the image filesystem). pip itself is never invoked at container
#    runtime. Both CVEs require running pip/setuptools against hostile input.

# msgpack — out-of-bounds read; only the vendored 1.1.2 under pip/_vendor
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# setuptools — path traversal in PackageIndex; only the vendored 70.3.0
CVE-2025-47273
